      "title": "What Is NgRx?",
      "lectureOrder": 685,
      "videoOrder": 630,
      "sourceHash": "979f8f0343355c20199fdd156d438d49647eda63570b463fa6e5a6bb8c752c41",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.31,
          "en": "So the effort to get started with this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.31,
          "end": 9.72,
          "en": "let's start with probably the most important question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.72,
          "end": 12.27,
          "en": "What is NgRx?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.27,
          "end": 16.71,
          "en": "And the answer is, it's a state management solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.71,
          "end": 18.81,
          "en": "It's a package you can install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.81,
          "end": 22.77,
          "en": "into your Angular projects to get some help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.77,
          "end": 26.16,
          "en": "with managing your application-wide state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.16,
          "end": 29.28,
          "en": "because that's what this NgRx package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.28,
          "end": 31.08,
          "en": "and library is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.08,
          "end": 33.81,
          "en": "It aims to help you with the management",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.81,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "of typically more complex application-wide state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 42.21,
          "en": "And state simply is data that's used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.21,
          "end": 45.6,
          "en": "in one or more components in your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.6,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "that typically changes over time, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 50.85,
          "en": "because the user clicked a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.85,
          "end": 54.45,
          "en": "And where those data changes should then lead to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.45,
          "end": 59.31,
          "en": "a change in the application, typically to a UI update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.31,
          "end": 62.25,
          "en": "And of course, in this course you already managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.25,
          "end": 65.7,
          "en": "a lot of state either directly in a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.7,
          "end": 67.53,
          "en": "by simply storing some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 70.11,
          "en": "in a property that then got changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.11,
          "end": 72.48,
          "en": "as a button was clicked, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.48,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "Or if you needed data in multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 79.62,
          "en": "with help of a service where you stored some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.62,
          "end": 82.59,
          "en": "in a service, changed it from component A,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.59,
          "end": 86.4,
          "en": "and then maybe used it in component B, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.4,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "with help of a behavior subject or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 92.7,
          "en": "So you already learned about state management",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.7,
          "end": 96.63,
          "en": "and NgRx is simply a never solution you could use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.63,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "instead of storing and managing your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 103.08,
          "en": "directly inside of components or services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.08,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "And the data for it is a totally optional solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "It's an alternative, not something you have to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 111.93,
          "en": "but something you might want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.93,
          "end": 113.88,
          "en": "in more complex applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.88,
          "end": 117.15,
          "en": "since, as you will learn in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.15,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "NgRx gives you a certain standardized,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 123.39,
          "en": "clearly defined approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.39,
          "end": 126.993,
          "en": "and way of managing application state.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
